WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:04.492
Scrooge wanted to refuse the ghost's invitation.

2
00:00:04.493 --> 00:00:08.740
He had no desire to walk anywhere with such a frightening creature!

3
00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:11.842
But it was pointless to resist.

4
00:00:11.843 --> 00:00:18.903
The ghost's grasp was as gentle as a child's hand, but it was stronger than the grip of any adult.

5
00:00:18.904 --> 00:00:22.994
The ghost pulled Scrooge toward one of the windows.

6
00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:25.789
"Wait, spirit!" Scrooge cried.

7
00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:29.820
"I'm a mortal, not a ghost, remember?

8
00:00:29.821 --> 00:00:36.491
And we're on the second floor. If I fall out the window, I'll get hurt!"

9
00:00:36.492 --> 00:00:40.401
"Don't worry," the ghost said.

10
00:00:40.402 --> 00:00:43.653
He touched Scrooge on his heart.

11
00:00:43.654 --> 00:00:49.861
"My touch on your heart is all it takes to keep you safe."

12
00:00:49.862 --> 00:00:55.513
With that, both spirit and Scrooge passed through the wall.

13
00:00:55.514 --> 00:01:01.567
Instead of emerging onto the street in front of the apartment building, they stood on an open road.

14
00:01:01.568 --> 00:01:04.430
The city and night had vanished.

15
00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:08.080
It was now a cold winter day in the country.

16
00:01:08.081 --> 00:01:14.819
Snowy fields lay on either side of the road, and the air felt clear and crisp.

17
00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:20.430
"Good heavens!" Scrooge cried, clasping his hands as he looked around.

18
00:01:20.431 --> 00:01:27.307
"I know exactly where we are. I grew up in this place!"

19
00:01:27.308 --> 00:01:32.169
The Ghost of Christmas Past touched Scrooge's heart again.

20
00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:37.481
Scrooge gasped as various pleasant odors floated past his nose.

21
00:01:37.482 --> 00:01:42.999
Each one reminded him of the few happy moments from his childhood.

22
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.978
There was the scent of his mother's lavender perfume.

23
00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:52.379
Then came the buttery aroma of the cookies his nanny had baked for him.

24
00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:58.992
Next he smelled the sweetness of his beloved sister's favorite candy.

25
00:01:58.993 --> 00:02:03.585
"Your lip is trembling," the ghost said in its mild voice.

26
00:02:03.586 --> 00:02:07.480
"And what is that upon your cheek?"

27
00:02:07.481 --> 00:02:11.611
Scrooge touched his cheek, which felt moist with tears.

28
00:02:11.612 --> 00:02:15.382
"Never mind," he said with a catch in his voice.

29
00:02:15.383 --> 00:02:19.131
"Lead me where you wish."

30
00:02:19.132 --> 00:02:23.915
"Don't you remember the way?" the spirit asked.

31
00:02:23.916 --> 00:02:28.235
"I do remember," Scrooge said.

32
00:02:28.236 --> 00:02:34.049
His feet carried him quickly along the road to a town.

33
00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:41.647
Scrooge recognized the bridge over the river, the church steeple, and everything else he saw.

34
00:02:41.648 --> 00:02:47.766
They passed a pair of shaggy ponies trotting along with laughing boys on their backs.

35
00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:54.541
Scrooge recognized the boys as well, though by now, they should be old men like him.

36
00:02:54.542 --> 00:03:00.358
He called out to them, but they didn't respond.

37
00:03:00.359 --> 00:03:05.460
"These people are shadows of things that have been," the ghost said.

38
00:03:05.461 --> 00:03:08.559
"They can't see or hear us."

39
00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:14.799
"I see," Scrooge said, watching more happy people go by.

40
00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:21.680
"Merry Christmas!" An older man tipped his hat to several young ladies.

41
00:03:21.681 --> 00:03:28.413
"And a merry Christmas to you, sir!" the ladies said with good cheer.

42
00:03:28.414 --> 00:03:34.349
Finally Scrooge reached a house that was even more familiar than the rest.

43
00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:40.385
In front of it, a young boy was building a snowman.

44
00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:48.273
Scrooge's eyes widened. "Why, that . . . that boy is me!"

45
00:03:48.274 --> 00:03:53.444
The young Ebenezer finished the snowman by placing a hat on its head.

46
00:03:53.445 --> 00:03:58.798
Then he grinned and ran into the house.

47
00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:04.474
A moment later he reappeared, pulling a laughing young woman by the hand.

48
00:04:04.475 --> 00:04:08.618
She was holding a baby wrapped in a blanket.

49
00:04:08.619 --> 00:04:11.396
"Oh," Scrooge whispered.

50
00:04:11.397 --> 00:04:15.622
"It's my mother—she's alive again.

51
00:04:15.623 --> 00:04:22.355
My beautiful, kind mother, and my dear little sister too."

52
00:04:22.356 --> 00:04:27.093
"Look, Mother!" Young Ebenezer was grinning proudly.

53
00:04:27.094 --> 00:04:31.180
"I built a snowman for baby Fan!"

54
00:04:31.181 --> 00:04:35.519
"It's wonderful, my clever son," Mother said.

55
00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:39.628
She held up the baby so tiny Fan could see too.

56
00:04:39.629 --> 00:04:44.478
The baby cooed and waved her plump arms.

57
00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:50.706
Suddenly a large man burst out of the house, scowling at the scene.

58
00:04:50.707 --> 00:04:56.375
"What's going on out here? It's far too cold to be outdoors without proper clothes!"

59
00:04:56.376 --> 00:05:00.265
"It's all right, darling," Mother said quickly.

60
00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.496
"I came out for only a moment.

61
00:05:02.497 --> 00:05:07.615
Ebenezer wanted to show his snowman to Fan and me. That's all."

62
00:05:07.616 --> 00:05:10.539
"Humbug!" the man snapped.

63
00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:13.316
"Ebenezer should be indoors, reading.

64
00:05:13.317 --> 00:05:19.701
What sort of businessman will he become while wasting time on silly activities like building snowmen?

65
00:05:19.702 --> 00:05:26.623
And is that my best hat?" His face turned red with outrage.

66
00:05:26.624 --> 00:05:33.295
Then he stomped over and grabbed the hat off the snowman, accidentally knocking off its head.

67
00:05:33.296 --> 00:05:39.985
"Get inside, all of you. If the baby gets sick, I'll blame you, boy!"

68
00:05:39.986 --> 00:05:43.479
Scrooge shuddered along with his younger self.

69
00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:53.063
"I remember that day," he said as he watched young Ebenezer slink back into the house behind his parents.

70
00:05:53.064 --> 00:05:59.004
"A short time later, my father sent me off to boarding school."

71
00:05:59.005 --> 00:06:06.327
The ghost nodded. "Come with me. We have much more to see."

72
00:06:06.328 --> 00:06:18.922
After one last glance at the sad, headless snowman, Scrooge obeyed.

